"""Lesson 12: frames missed by the JavaScript thread, and the two annotated examples."""
import json
from fig import Fig

T = {
 "en": dict(aria="Six frames of 16.7 milliseconds each, from 0 to 100 milliseconds. The JavaScript thread is busy with a render from about 25 to 65 milliseconds. An animation driven from JavaScript delivers frames 1, 2, 5 and 6 and misses frames 3 and 4, so the previous picture stays on screen. The same animation run on the UI thread delivers all six frames.",
   js="JavaScript thread", busy="busy: a render", fromjs="animation driven", fromjs2="from JavaScript", ui="animation run", ui2="on the UI thread",
   missed="missed", ok="drawn", cap="A frame is due every 16.7 ms whatever JavaScript is doing. While it is busy, an animation that waits for it misses frames; one handed to the UI thread does not."),
 "pt": dict(aria="Seis quadros de 16,7 milissegundos cada, de 0 a 100 milissegundos. A thread do JavaScript está ocupada com uma renderização de mais ou menos 25 a 65 milissegundos. Uma animação conduzida pelo JavaScript entrega os quadros 1, 2, 5 e 6 e perde os quadros 3 e 4, e a imagem anterior fica na tela. A mesma animação rodando na thread de UI entrega os seis quadros.",
   js="thread do JavaScript", busy="ocupada: uma renderização", fromjs="animação conduzida", fromjs2="pelo JavaScript", ui="animação rodando", ui2="na thread de UI",
   missed="perdido", ok="desenhado", cap="Um quadro é devido a cada 16,7 ms, faça o JavaScript o que fizer. Enquanto ele está ocupado, uma animação que espera por ele perde quadros; uma entregue à thread de UI, não."),
}

X0, PX = 170, 5.2  # where 0 ms is, and pixels per millisecond


def figures(lang):
    t = T[lang]
    f = Fig("l12-threads", 720, 250, t["aria"])
    for i in range(7):
        ms = i * 100 / 6
        x = X0 + ms * PX
        f.arrow([(x, 36), (x, 46)], color="wire", head=False, width=1)
        f.text(x, 28, f"{round(ms)} ms", mono=True, size=9, fill="paper-dim")
    f.text(150, 70, t["js"], anchor="end", size=9.5)
    f.rect(X0 + 25 * PX, 56, 40 * PX, 28, stroke="amber", fill="panel")
    f.text(X0 + 45 * PX, 70, t["busy"], size=9.5, fill="amber")
    f.text(150, 122, t["fromjs"], anchor="end", size=9.5)
    f.text(150, 135, t["fromjs2"], anchor="end", size=9.5)
    f.text(150, 182, t["ui"], anchor="end", size=9.5)
    f.text(150, 195, t["ui2"], anchor="end", size=9.5)
    for i in range(6):
        x = X0 + (i * 100 / 6) * PX + 6
        w = (100 / 6) * PX - 12
        missed = i in (2, 3)
        f.rect(x, 112, w, 34, stroke="amber" if missed else "phosphor", fill="panel", dashed=missed)
        f.text(x + w / 2, 129, t["missed"] if missed else t["ok"], size=8.5, fill="amber" if missed else "phosphor", italic=missed)
        f.rect(x, 172, w, 34, stroke="phosphor", fill="panel")
        f.text(x + w / 2, 189, t["ok"], size=8.5, fill="phosphor")
    return {"l12-threads": f.json(caption=t["cap"])}



EXAMPLES = {'reanimated': [{'language': 'tsx', 'file': 'src/WeekBarReanimated.tsx', 'parts': [('// src/WeekBarReanimated.tsx: the week bar again, with the animation written for Reanimated.\nimport { useEffect, useState } from "react";\nimport { StyleSheet, View } from "react-native";\nimport Animated, {\n  Easing,\n  ReduceMotion,\n  useAnimatedStyle,\n  useSharedValue,\n  withTiming,\n} from "react-native-reanimated";\nimport { useTheme } from "./theme";\n\ntype Props = { done: number; planned: number };\n', 'The imports are the whole vocabulary: a value both threads can read, a style computed from it, and an animation that moves it.', 'Os imports são o vocabulário todo: um valor que as duas threads leem, um estilo calculado a partir dele e uma animação que o move.'), ('export function WeekBar({ done, planned }: Props) {\n  const t = useTheme();\n  const share = planned > 0 ? done / planned : 0;\n  const scale = useSharedValue(share);\n  const [width, setWidth] = useState(0);', '`useSharedValue` takes the place of `useRef(new Animated.Value(...))`. It is created once, like the ref, and it lives where the UI thread can read it.', 'O `useSharedValue` toma o lugar de `useRef(new Animated.Value(...))`. É criado uma vez, como o ref, e mora onde a thread de UI consegue lê-lo.'), ('  useEffect(() => {\n    scale.value = withTiming(share, {\n      duration: 300,\n      easing: Easing.out(Easing.cubic),\n      reduceMotion: ReduceMotion.System,\n    });\n  }, [share, scale]);', "Assigning an animation to `.value` starts it. `ReduceMotion.System` follows the phone's setting by itself, so the question the `Animated` version asked by hand is gone.", 'Atribuir uma animação a `.value` a inicia. `ReduceMotion.System` segue sozinho a configuração do celular, e a pergunta que a versão com `Animated` fazia à mão some.'), ('  const grown = useAnimatedStyle(() => ({\n    transform: [{ translateX: -width / 2 }, { scaleX: scale.value }, { translateX: width / 2 }],\n  }));', "This function is a **worklet**: Reanimated's Babel plugin copies it to the UI thread, which runs it on every frame and sets the transform without asking JavaScript. `width` is copied along with it each time the component renders.", 'Esta função é um **worklet**: o plugin de Babel do Reanimated a copia para a thread de UI, que a roda a cada quadro e define a transformação sem perguntar ao JavaScript. O `width` é copiado junto a cada renderização do componente.'), ('  return (\n    <View\n      accessible\n      role="progressbar"\n      aria-label="Minutes done this week"\n      aria-valuemin={0}\n      aria-valuemax={planned}\n      aria-valuenow={done}\n      onLayout={(e) => setWidth(e.nativeEvent.layout.width)}\n      style={[styles.track, { backgroundColor: t.track }]}\n    >\n      <Animated.View style={[styles.done, { width, backgroundColor: t.accent }, grown]} />\n    </View>\n  );\n}\n\nconst styles = StyleSheet.create({\n  track: { height: 12, borderRadius: 6, overflow: "hidden" },\n  done: { height: 12 },\n});', 'The rest is the same component: the same track, the same accessible values. Only the animated style changed hands.', 'O resto é o mesmo componente: a mesma trilha, os mesmos valores acessíveis. Só o estilo animado mudou de mãos.')]}], 'gestures': [{'language': 'tsx', 'file': 'src/SwipeRow.tsx', 'parts': [('// src/SwipeRow.tsx: a row that follows a finger to the left and, dragged far enough, marks itself done.\n// The row\'s own button does the same thing; the swipe is a shortcut, never the only way.\nimport type { ReactNode } from "react";\nimport { GestureDetector, usePanGesture } from "react-native-gesture-handler";\nimport Animated, { useAnimatedStyle, useSharedValue, withSpring } from "react-native-reanimated";\nimport { scheduleOnRN } from "react-native-worklets";\nimport { swipeCompletes } from "./swipe";\n\ntype Props = { onDone: () => void; children: ReactNode };\n', 'Three libraries meet here: the gesture comes from Gesture Handler, the movement from Reanimated, and the way back to JavaScript from Worklets.', 'Três bibliotecas se encontram aqui: o gesto vem do Gesture Handler, o movimento do Reanimated e o caminho de volta ao JavaScript do Worklets.'), ('export function SwipeRow({ onDone, children }: Props) {\n  const x = useSharedValue(0);', '`x` is how far the row has moved. It starts at 0 and only the UI thread changes it while the finger is down.', 'O `x` é quanto a linha andou. Começa em 0, e só a thread de UI o muda enquanto o dedo está na tela.'), ('  const pan = usePanGesture({\n    activeOffsetX: [-12, 12],', 'A **pan** is a finger that moves. `activeOffsetX` makes it wait until the finger has gone 12 points sideways before it claims the touch, so a vertical scroll through the list still scrolls.', 'Um **pan** é um dedo que se move. O `activeOffsetX` o faz esperar até o dedo andar 12 pontos para o lado antes de tomar o toque, e assim uma rolagem vertical pela lista continua rolando.'), ('    onUpdate: (e) => {\n      x.value = Math.min(0, e.translationX);\n    },', 'Called on every movement, on the UI thread. `translationX` is the distance from where the finger landed; `Math.min` lets the row go left and never right.', 'Chamado a cada movimento, na thread de UI. O `translationX` é a distância desde onde o dedo pousou; o `Math.min` deixa a linha ir para a esquerda e nunca para a direita.'), ('    onDeactivate: (e) => {\n      if (swipeCompletes(e.translationX)) scheduleOnRN(onDone);\n      x.value = withSpring(0);\n    },\n  });', "Called once when the finger lifts. The decision is a worklet, so it can run here; `onDone` is the planner's ordinary function, so `scheduleOnRN` hands it to the JavaScript thread. Either way the row springs back: the list redraws it as done if the server agrees.", 'Chamado uma vez, quando o dedo sobe. A decisão é um worklet, então pode rodar aqui; o `onDone` é uma função comum do planner, então o `scheduleOnRN` a entrega à thread do JavaScript. Nos dois casos a linha volta com uma mola: a lista a redesenha como feita se o servidor concordar.'), ('  const moved = useAnimatedStyle(() => ({ transform: [{ translateX: x.value }] }));\n  return (\n    <GestureDetector gesture={pan}>\n      <Animated.View style={moved}>{children}</Animated.View>\n    </GestureDetector>\n  );\n}', '`GestureDetector` attaches the gesture to the view inside it. The style follows `x` on every frame with no render, which is the point of all this.', 'O `GestureDetector` prende o gesto à view de dentro. O estilo acompanha o `x` a cada quadro sem renderização, que é o motivo disso tudo.')]}]}
